From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:54:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 62/68] hottyterm: motion paces to the display's refresh rate

Pass hotty-blitz the refresh rate of the display the window is on, through
hotty_host_set_refresh_rate, so that CSS animations and fading scrollbars
ask for frames at it rather than at 60 Hz. GTK watches the widget's
GdkSurface (realize, unrealize), the monitors it enters and leaves, and the
monitor's refresh-rate. AppKit sends the screen's rate (1 over its
minimumRefreshInterval, or its maximumFramesPerSecond) as the window
changes screens, as its backing properties change, and as the screen
parameters change. The rate is kept before the lazy host exists, and 0 for
a rate not known is hotty-blitz's 60 Hz. The log says when the host is
handed a rate.

Adds 23 lines to upstream files: two GTK lifecycle hooks, the namespaced
embedded C bridge and its header declaration, and AppKit hooks. Host logic
stays in src/termio/hotty.zig.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
